menu "Michi Music Stream State"

    config MICHI_STATE_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Event queue length (events)"
        default 16
        range 4 256
        help
          Depth of the FreeRTOS queue between producers (post/post_from_isr/
          request) and the FSM task. Events dropped while the queue is full
          return ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT to the producer and are counted: the FSM
          task logs the accumulated count periodically, and task-context
          producers log their own drop. Keep the value high enough for the
          busiest burst (e.g. a session teardown storm in phase 12).

    config MICHI_STATE_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "State machine task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 16384
        help
          Stack of the FSM task (ESP-IDF xTaskCreate takes bytes). The task
          only receives, logs and dispatches, so the default is generous;
          raise it only if a future observer grows the dispatch frame.

    config MICHI_STATE_MAX_OBSERVERS
        int "Maximum event observers"
        default 8
        range 1 32
        help
          Capacity of the observer table (one per registered (filter, fn)
          pair). Phase consumers: display (6), LED (7), network (9), audio
          (11), API (12). Registration beyond the limit fails with
          ESP_ERR_NO_MEM.

endmenu
